# Host-local accepted migration debt for the gh/git adapter ratchet (G-ADAPTER).
# theory-selfgrowth is a HOST package: it cannot reach forge.github (forge is a
# platform-internal, unpublishable library — a hard framework gate). Its propose department
# must therefore construct one raw `gh issue list` read to self-search its own prior
# frontier-request markers (generation-scoped dedup + open-request exclusion, #296/#339).
# Issue-create egress stays with github-proxy.
#
# NORTH-STAR (retire this entry): petition upstream for a narrow, publishable github-proxy
# read/search-by-marker event pair, symmetric to its existing write-side issue-create — a
# generic capability every host self-dedup producer needs. When that lands, this producer
# switches to it and this allowlist file is deleted.
packages/theory-selfgrowth/departments/propose/main.lua:
- gh issue
